    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Spacious detached family home circa 210m2 with attached garage 20m2 set on 0.5 acres of mature, landscaped gardens, gazebo & patio area to the rear. The property has a tarmac driveway, oil fired heating, electric charging point and double-glazed windows & doors. \r\nIt is located in a scenic area with views of the Galty mountains, just outside Rossadrehid village and just 5mins drive to Bansha,15mins Cahir, Clonmel 30 mins and Limerick 55 minutes on the N24."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hall with timber floor\r\nLiving room with bay window, solid fuel stove &double doors leading to kitchen/dining room.\r\nSitting room with carpet floor, picture window side door leading to the garden, stove with marble & cast-iron fireplace and decorative coving.\r\nKitchen/ dining area with solid wood fitted kitchen, island unit and feature rangemaster cooker with timber over mantle.\r\nUtility room & wc plumbed for washing machine & with fitted units. Door leading to rear driveway and garden\r\nOffice with double windows accessed via the utility room\r\nFirst floor-\r\nLarge spacious landing area with picture window allowing for scenic views of the mountains.\r\nBedroom one with timber floor\r\nBedroom two with timber floor\r\nBedroom three with carpet floor\r\nMaster bedroom with bay window and en suite\r\nBathroom with bath and separate shower."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Large spacious detached property\r\nlandscaped gardens with mature trees & shrubs\r\nTarmac Driveway\r\nThe property has an attached garage with scrolling rolling door. There is a covered gazebo area providing an outdoor area for all year round entertaining along with a patio area accessed via steps from the garden.\r\n It is surrounded by mature trees and shrubs and has commanding views of the Galty Mountains and Lake Muskry. This picturesque setting is ideal for those interested in outdoor pursuits and hillwalking all just a short stroll away"
      },
      {
